:: D01_NovaCure [nobr]
<<HUD>>

<<if not $dressedDay1>>

<div class="prose-block">
<p>I&apos;m not walking into Meridian Tower like this. Not in whatever I&apos;m currently wearing, or barely wearing. I need to get dressed first.</p>
</div>

<div class="choice-block" style="margin-top:2rem;">
	<<link '<span>← Back outside</span>' "Outside">><</link>>
</div>

<<else>>

<<SceneDivider "The Bus">>

<<ImagePlaceholder "Bus interior, a man's gaze traveling down toward her legs" "banner" "assets/locations/misc/bus-male-gaze.png">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>Back seat of the bus, hood up, knees pressed together in an adjustment I didn&apos;t consciously choose. My body just made it automatically, the way my skeleton sits now when I&apos;m not thinking about it. Wider hips, thighs touching, knees together.</p>

<p>A man in the middle of the bus turns and looks at me. His eyes start at my face, or whatever he can see of it under the hood, and travel down toward my legs. The joggers have ridden up, showing my ankle, smooth, pale, unmistakably female.</p>

<p>I pull the fabric down and tuck my ankles under the seat. He turns back around.</p>

<p>That&apos;s the male gaze. I spent twenty years on the other side of it, never whistling at women on the street, never staring on buses, never trying to make anyone uncomfortable on purpose. But I knew it existed. I understood it theoretically. I never understood it as a frequency that actually vibrates through your skin and makes you want to fold yourself into the smallest possible shape.</p>

<p>Now I understand it.</p>

<p>NovaCure again. Sixth floor, Suite 604, the same sterile hallway, the same waiting room, the same potted plant that might still be fake.</p>

<p>Nurse Patel comes out and sees me. Her professional mask holds, but her eyes widen for a fraction of a second, just a flash, and then it&apos;s gone.</p>

<<Dialogue "Nurse Patel" "👩‍⚕️" "...Marcus?" "">>
<<Dialogue "You" "😶" "Yeah." "you">>

<p>She doesn&apos;t ask any follow-up questions. &quot;Okay. Let&apos;s get you into an exam room.&quot;</p>

</div>

<<SceneDivider "Examination">>

<<ImagePlaceholder "Exam room, stirrups visible, Dr. Amelia with a tablet" "banner" "assets/locations/novacure/exam-room-stirrups.png">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>The examination room is the same one from last night. The paper on the table crinkles when I sit down. My feet dangle, I&apos;m three inches shorter now and the table hasn&apos;t changed height.</p>

<p>Nurse Patel takes my vitals. Weight, 128 pounds, I&apos;ve lost twenty pounds overnight. Height, five-six, down three inches. Blood pressure elevated. Heart rate 92, anxiety probably. She doesn&apos;t comment on any of it, just writes it down.</p>

<p>Dr. Amelia walks in.</p>

<p>She looks at me, and here&apos;s the thing that makes my blood run cold: she doesn&apos;t look surprised at all. No visible shock on her face, no &quot;oh my God,&quot; no widening of the eyes. Nurse Patel flinched, a human reaction, quickly masked. Dr. Amelia doesn&apos;t flinch. Dr. Amelia looks at me the way you&apos;d look at a spreadsheet that returned exactly the result you expected.</p>

<<Dialogue "Dr. Amelia" "🥼" "Remove your clothes, please. You can keep the undergarments." "">>

<p>I strip down, hoodie off, t-shirt off, standing in the cold room in bunched-up boxers that are trying to fall off my hips. My arms cross over my breasts on instinct. Goosebumps rise across every inch of new skin.</p>

<p>She examines me clinically. Her hands palpate my breasts and I flinch, they&apos;re sensitive, her cold fingers on the new tissue send a jolt through me I wasn&apos;t prepared for.</p>

<<Dialogue "Dr. Amelia" "🥼" "B-cup. Well-formed." "">>

<p>She says it to her tablet, not to me. She measures my waist, my hips, notes down the numbers without a single word of commentary.</p>

<<Dialogue "Dr. Amelia" "🥼" "I need to examine your genitalia. Please lie on the table and place your feet in the stirrups." "">>

<p>I look at the table. Metal arms at the end, splayed out like insect legs, padded foot rests waiting. Stirrups. I&apos;ve seen them on TV before. I never once imagined my own feet in them.</p>

<<Dialogue "You" "😳" "You're fucking kidding." "you">>

<p>She is not kidding, not even a little.</p>

<p>I lie back. The paper crinkles under me. I place my feet in the stirrups and let my legs fall open. The boxers get pulled down. I&apos;m exposed, spread open under fluorescent light, in the most vulnerable position I have ever been in. The position half the world goes through for routine checkups. The position I never once thought about as a man. The position I&apos;m in right now while a woman in a lab coat inserts a cold metal speculum into a vagina I&apos;ve had for less than twelve hours.</p>

<p>I grip the edges of the table. Tears leak from the corners of my eyes, not from pain, the speculum is uncomfortable but not painful, but from the overwhelming totality of the whole thing. From the sound of the speculum clicking open. From the fact that I have something inside me for it to open at all.</p>

<<Dialogue "Dr. Amelia" "🥼" "Vaginal canal present and fully formed. Approximately 5.5 inches depth. Cervix visible and healthy. Lubrication response normal." "">>

<<Dialogue "You" "😢" "Can you PLEASE talk about my body like I'm in the room?" "you">>

<p>She pauses and looks at me over the speculum, those cold blue-grey eyes behind the frameless glasses. For one single beat something passes through them. Guilt, maybe. Recognition. I can&apos;t quite tell, and it&apos;s gone before I can name it properly.</p>

<<Dialogue "Dr. Amelia" "🥼" "I apologize. You have a fully functional female reproductive system. Ovaries, uterus, fallopian tubes, all present and healthy." "">>

<p>She removes the speculum carefully. &quot;You are, by every biological metric, female.&quot;</p>

</div>

<<SceneDivider "The Confrontation">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>I&apos;m dressed again, the hoodie and joggers swallowing me whole, sitting on the exam table. Dr. Amelia stands across from me holding her tablet like a shield.</p>

<<Dialogue "You" "😠" "Change me back." "you">>

<<Dialogue "Dr. Amelia" "🥼" "We are investigating the mechanism of transformation. Reversal is not currently available." "">>

<<Dialogue "You" "😠" "NOT CURRENTLY?" "you">>

<<Dialogue "Dr. Amelia" "🥼" "You signed Form 7-C, clause 12(b). Unforeseen physiological outcomes. The consent was..." "">>

<p>&quot;I signed up for a PILL TRIAL.&quot; My voice, this new voice, higher and thinner, cracks on the word &quot;trial.&quot; &quot;Not a sex change. Not a... not THIS. I was a MAN yesterday. I had a DICK yesterday. You can&apos;t just... you have to...&quot;</p>

<<Dialogue "Dr. Amelia" "🥼" "I understand your distress." "">>

<p>&quot;You don&apos;t understand SHIT. You&apos;re standing there with your clipboard and your lab coat and you don&apos;t look surprised. You don&apos;t even look SURPRISED.&quot;</p>

<p>The silence after that is thick enough to drown in. Dr. Amelia adjusts her glasses.</p>

<<Dialogue "Dr. Amelia" "🥼" "NovaCure is prepared to offer support during this period of adjustment." "">>

<p>Support. That&apos;s the word she uses. Here&apos;s what NovaCure&apos;s idea of support actually looks like.</p>

<p>New legal identification, already prepared, an updated driver&apos;s license, a Social Security amendment, an updated school record. The name change is technically optional. Their default suggestion is Mia Cole, though I can choose my own if I want. They have a form for that. They have an actual form for turning a man into a woman and issuing all the new paperwork to match.</p>

<p>Updated medical records reflecting my new female biology.</p>

<p>$800 a month, a &quot;participant stipend&quot; for six months, framed as support and functioning as hush money.</p>

<p>Monthly check-ins, plus Dr. Amelia&apos;s direct line &quot;for emergencies.&quot;</p>

<p>I take the new ID card, then the driver&apos;s license clipped behind it. Nurse Patel took the photo five minutes ago, me sitting on the exam table, shell-shocked, hair a total mess, drowning in a hoodie three sizes too big. The woman in that photo has my eyes and my freckles and nothing else I recognize at all.</p>

<p>The name on both cards reads: <<print $player.name>> Cole.</p>

</div>

<<ImagePlaceholder "Close-up of the new civic ID card, trembling hands" "float" "assets/items/misc/new-female-id.png">>
<<ImagePlaceholder "Close-up of the new driver's license, trembling hands" "float" "assets/items/misc/new-female-driver-license.png">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>I stare at them, thinking about how quickly they processed all this, how ready they already were. Two cards, two photos, all the paperwork, the exact stipend amount, every bit of it prepared and waiting. Almost like they expected this. Almost like this was the whole point.</p>

<<Dialogue "Dr. Amelia" "🥼" "We'll see you in two weeks for your first check-in. Call the direct line if you experience anything unusual." "">>

<p>Everything is unusual right now. I am the unusual thing sitting in this room, and I want to scream that at her. Instead I put the cards in my pocket and walk out on legs three inches shorter than yesterday, then take the elevator down in a body I never once asked for.</p>

</div>

<div class="choice-block">
	<<link '<span>🏙️ Head back outside</span>' "District_Central">>
		<<set $metDrAmelia to true>>
		<<set $metNursePatel to true>>
		<<set $novaCureVisitCount += 1>>
		<<set $player.money += 800>>
		<<set $income.novacure += 800>>
		<<set $timeslot to "Evening">>
		<<set $player.stress to Math.clamp($player.stress + 5, 0, 100)>>
		<<set $novaCureDay1Done to true>>
		<<run window.rbAddJournalEntry("Confirmed", "Fully female, by every biological metric Dr. Amelia could name. No reversal available. $800 a month, a new ID, and a direct line \"for emergencies.\" Her name is Mia Cole now.")>>
	<</link>>
</div>

<</if>>
